==Acquisition==
*This mod can be acquired by attaining the rank of '''General''' under {{Faction|Steel Meridian}}, or the rank of '''Exalted''' under {{Faction|Red Veil}}, and spending {{sc|25,000}} to purchase.

==Notes==
*When casting {{A|Shroud of Dynar}}, one random enemy within a '''25''' meter radius will be marked by flowing energy. This enemy receives increased Damage Vulnerability. 
**Targeting radius is '''not''' affected by mods.
**Damage Vulnerability is affected by [[Ability Strength]].
**The targeted enemy is highlighted through terrain.
**The energy colour is dependent on the selected Warframe energy colour.
*Upon the death of the targeted enemy, a new enemy will be targeted ''if'' Shroud of Dynar's invisibility is still active.
**A new enemy will '''not''' be targeted otherwise, even if Shroud of Dynar's melee buff is still active.
*Casting {{A|Fangs of Raksh}} on the targeted enemy will confer a bonus on its spread radius upon the enemy's death.
**Spread radius bonus is '''not''' affected by mods but is multiplicative with [[Ability Range]] mods.
***For example, using a maxed {{M|Stretch}} and Prey of Dynar results in:<br />{{MathText|Total spread radius {{eql}} Base spread radius {{mul}} (1 + Prey of Dynar Bonus) {{mul}} (1 + Range Mods)}} <br>{{Math|{{eql}} 7 {{mul}} (1 + {{M|Prey of Dynar|1.5}}) {{mul}} {{M|Stretch|1.45}}|t=y|bf=y}}
**Spread radius bonus expires upon the end of Shroud of Dynar.

==Tips==
*Using {{A|Ulfrun's Descent}} allows for more than one enemy to be targeted for the duration of Shroud of Dynar as its attacks do not end the invisibility phase.
*A bright colour for Voruna's energy should be chosen as it may otherwise be difficult to spot the targeted enemy.
*Equipping the augment makes it easier to keep {{A|Lycath's Hunt}} active due to the large increase in range.
*Since Damage Vulnerability is not affected by mod rank, it may be beneficial to equip an unranked copy to reduce drain if one isn't interested in the spread radius bonus.

==Bugs==
*Can highlight security cameras in Corpus ships/similar, despite those entities being untargetable by {{A|Fangs of Raksh}}

